<h2>The pitch multiplier</h2>
<p>A sloped roof has more surface than the ground it covers. The multiplier is √(1 + (rise ÷ 12)²): a 6/12 roof is about 11.8% larger than its footprint, an 8/12 roof about 20.2% larger, and a 12/12 roof about 41.4% larger. Leave that out and a 30-square roof can be written as 25.</p>
<h2>What to compare in the carrier’s estimate</h2>
<ul><li>Total squares and the waste percentage on the shingle line.</li><li>Steep charges (often starting at 7/12) and high-roof charges for two-story sections.</li><li>Separate lines for starter, ridge cap, drip edge, valley metal and ice-and-water shield.</li><li>Removal, felt or synthetic underlayment, and decking replacement where boards are damaged.</li></ul>
<p>Differences of more than 5–10% in squares deserve a closer look. Hail and wind claims in North Mississippi and the Pine Belt often turn on exactly these lines — see our <a href="/our-appraisal-services/roof-hail-claim-appraisal/">roof and hail claim appraisal</a> page.</p>
<h2>Limits of a footprint method</h2>
<p>Roofs with several pitches, dormers and valleys should be measured plane by plane, from an aerial report or in the field. Use this calculator as a sanity check, not a replacement for measurement.</p>
<h2>About this calculator</h2><div class="faqs"><details><summary>What is a roofing square?</summary><p>One hundred square feet of roof surface. Many single-story Mississippi homes fall between 20 and 35 squares.</p></details><details><summary>Why does the waste factor change with roof shape?</summary><p>Hips, valleys and dormers need more cutting, so more material ends up as scrap. Simple gables waste the least.</p></details></div><h2>More free calculators</h2><div class="rel"><a class="rel-card" href="/claim-calculator-suite/named-storm-deductible-calculator/"><small>Calculator</small><span>Named-Storm Deductible Calculator</span><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel-card" href="/claim-calculator-suite/claim-calendar-builder/"><small>Planner</small><span>Claim Calendar Builder</span><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a><a class="rel-card" href="/claim-calculator-suite/appraisal-readiness-checkup/"><small>Checklist</small><span>Appraisal Readiness Checkup</span><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></div></article><aside class="side"><div class="side-in"><div class="side-box side-call"><h2 class="side-h">Talk it through first</h2><p>Free first conversation. We’ll tell you plainly whether appraisal fits your claim.</p><a class="side-phone" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg class="ico" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="roun